From 615d439f4a83a8e831661d49ee265e9fe139bf17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:00:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(routing): honour committed switch intents in
 commit order, one event each

Why-chain (five whys, evidence: deleg_d342c5fe review probe4.log at 24096f5d558):
1. Next exact build on the newer pick raised "Exact pinned route cannot fail over":
   the durable allocation held the OLDER pick's tuple.
2. A build that read intent A allocated after a newer intent B was already honoured;
   fence(A) != fence(B), so the allocator replaced again with A's tuple.
3. The switch_fences row was an equality fence (last token per root/class) with no order,
   and the read -> allocate window is not serialized against later switches (cold
   /review vs the drained queued turn).
4. Intent rows had no event identity: the same tuple+generation recorded again (profile
   selection A -> B -> A writes the same runtime_generation) produced the same token,
   mistaken for the honoured one after an unfenced in-session switch.
5. Not caught: fence tests covered same-intent overlap, crash retry and rollback, never
   an older intent allocating after a newer one, nor a repeated identical intent.

Fix: record_in_transaction stamps each intent with an event {store nonce, seq} from one
counter in the session store, taken in the recording transaction (unique, commit
ordered; signature unchanged, so the canonical writers are untouched). fence_token
encodes it; the allocator replaces only when supersedes(token, honoured): same store ->
strictly newer seq; equal -> sticky (retry / overlap); legacy or cross-store -> the old
equality fence. A superseded build now takes the sticky path (an exact pin refuses it)
and cannot move the newer pin. Failed prepare still rolls the fence back; unfenced
replace=True unchanged. replace is typed bool | str through resolve_model_route,
resolve_class_runtime, resolve_managed_runtime and RoutingState, matching
hermes_cli/runtime_provider.

Tests: tests/agent/test_route_switch_intent_order.py (real AIAgent builds: stale older
after newer, repeated identical intent after unfenced switch, rollback then crash retry
then newer intent; token order units). Two real-build tests fail at 24096f5d558.
